    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0228" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4137</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Russia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-01T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1917—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1367. Your 1231, April 28. Please say to Milyukov that this Government will be
                    delighted to receive commission from Russia, and that it is believed that good
                    results would follow from the visit of the commission at as early a date as
                    possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
